# Copy to .env (gitignored). Never commit real values.
# Every line starts with # on purpose: remove the # and fill in the value. An empty KEY= counts as not set.
# Host-only (uv run cvboost). In Docker the DB path is fixed to /data/cvboost.sqlite by compose.
# CVBOOST_DB=
# CVBOOST_LOG_LEVEL=
# TZ=
# LLM via your own Claude subscription. CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is needed only in
# Docker/VPS (from `claude setup-token`); on the Mac the keychain login is used.
# Do NOT put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here: it is never passed to claude and an api_key login is refused.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Telegram alerts. Only here, never in git; the token is never logged.
# Create the bot in @BotFather, message it /start once, then set both values.
# Run ONE worker per bot (Mac or VPS, not both).
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# Web panel: `uv run cvboost web` -> http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Basic auth is optional locally; set BOTH or neither. Required if the panel listens on a
# non-loopback address without CVBOOST_WEB_TRUST_NETWORK=1.
# CVBOOST_WEB_USER=
# CVBOOST_WEB_PASSWORD=
# Comma-separated Host names the panel answers to (anything else gets 400: DNS-rebinding guard).
# CVBOOST_WEB_HOSTS=
# Fixed CSRF signing key (>= 32 random chars); without it tokens last until a restart.
# CVBOOST_WEB_SECRET=
# Where CVBoost writes application kits (default: <dir of CVBOOST_DB>/kits).
# CVBOOST_KITS_DIR=

# Alerts mailbox: read-only IMAP of the dedicated Gmail (App password). Set BOTH or neither.
# CVBOOST_IMAP_USER=
# CVBOOST_IMAP_PASSWORD=
# CVBOOST_IMAP_HOST=
# CVBOOST_IMAP_MAILBOX=
# Your own addresses whose manually forwarded mails are unwrapped (default: none).
# CVBOOST_MAIL_FORWARDERS=

# Keyed job sources (optional; see SOURCES.md for where to get each key). Without a key the source
# stays idle.
# ADZUNA_APP_ID=
# ADZUNA_APP_KEY=
# REED_API_KEY=
# ITJOBS_API_KEY=
